mixin () {
  /// Return the backend API documentation as static Markdown.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# MIRAGE Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThe MIRAGE backend serves the MIRAGE fragrance house storefront. It exposes a read-only fragrance catalogue and a demo checkout that prices orders from that same catalogue. There is no real payment processing and no customer account or order history: `placeOrder` validates and prices a request and returns the resulting order, but does not persist it.\n\n## Public methods\n\n### `listFragrances() : query -> [Fragrance]`\nReturns every fragrance in the catalogue. Anonymous callers are allowed.\n\n### `getFragrance(id : FragranceId) : query -> ?Fragrance`\nReturns the fragrance with the given id, or `null` when no such fragrance exists. Anonymous callers are allowed.\n\n### `placeOrder(delivery : DeliveryDetails, items : [OrderItemRequest]) : async Result<Order, OrderError>`\nValidates and prices a demo order. Any caller is accepted, including anonymous ones: the caller principal is read from the message but ignored, so no sign-in is required. The order is not stored; the returned `Order` is the only record of it.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : query -> Text`\nReturns this document.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\n- `listFragrances`, `getFragrance` and `getApiDoc` are open to any caller, including anonymous ones.\n- `placeOrder` accepts any caller, including anonymous ones. The caller principal is read from the message but ignored (`ignore caller`): orders are not associated with an account and are not persisted, so no signed-in caller is required.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- The backend includes the shared authorization mixin, which manages roles and registration. A direct API caller registers by calling `_initialize_access_control()` once as a signed-in (non-anonymous) caller before any role-guarded call; signing in through the app's own frontend registers the caller the same way. The first non-anonymous caller to register becomes `#admin`; every later non-anonymous caller becomes `#user`. Anonymous callers are ignored and receive no role.\n- Registration happens only when a caller signs in through the app's own frontend or calls `_initialize_access_control()`, so a principal that never did so is unregistered even when it belongs to the app's owner, and a signed-in caller derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered.\n- `getCallerUserRole()` returns `#guest` for an anonymous caller and traps with `User is not registered` for a signed-in caller that has not registered. The catalogue and checkout endpoints above do not require a registered role.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `FragranceId` and `OrderId` are `Nat`.\n- `Price` is a `Nat` in whole currency units (no minor units, no decimals).\n- `quantity` is a `Nat`; a quantity of `0` is rejected.\n- `sizeLabel` is a `Text` that must exactly match a size label in the catalogue (for example `\"50 ML\"`, uppercase with a space).\n- `notes` and `sizes` are arrays; `sizes` is ordered as declared in the catalogue.\n- `OrderError` is a variant: `#emptyOrder`, `#unknownFragrance(FragranceId)`, `#unknownSize({ fragranceId; sizeLabel })`, `#invalidQuantity({ fragranceId; sizeLabel })`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- The catalogue is static and deterministic: every call returns the same data, so no polling is required.\n- `placeOrder` is a single request/response call. There is no asynchronous job, no order status to poll, and no completion condition beyond the returned `Result`.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `placeOrder` does not persist anything, so retrying it is safe: a repeated call returns an equivalent order with a new id. It has no destructive side effects and no duplicate-call hazard.\n- Order ids are assigned from a transient counter that resets on canister upgrade; ids are therefore not stable across upgrades and must not be treated as durable identifiers.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- `placeOrder` returns `#err` for caller-fixable problems (empty order, unknown fragrance, unknown size, zero quantity) rather than trapping, so callers should branch on the `OrderError` variant.\n- Prices are resolved from the shared catalogue, so order totals always match the catalogue prices.\n- The catalogue is not persisted actor state and is not exposed through the query layer; it is served only through `listFragrances` and `getFragrance`.\n";
  };
};
